IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-seat`

-- Cases for oa1-seat: at least one case per question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the
-- text of the section named in the comment beside the assertion; none is copied from the encoding's output.


§ `Old Age Security Act, Part I -- the questions of a person who is 65 or older (or about to be) about the pension`

§§ `Do I qualify for a pension?`
-- Born 1960, 45 years of residence after 18: 3(1)(c) (65, not a pensioner in 1977, at least forty years).
#ASSERT `s 3(1): Am I qualified for a full monthly pension` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 45 TRUE
-- 30 years of residence: short of forty, and too young to have met 3(1)(b)(i) in 1977.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1): Am I qualified for a full monthly pension` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 30 TRUE)
-- Born 1950: 27 in 1977, living in Canada then, 76 now, ten years of residence just before approval: 3(1)(b).
#ASSERT `s 3(1): Am I qualified for a full monthly pension` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 30 TRUE
-- A pensioner on July 1, 1977: 3(1)(a).
#ASSERT `s 3(1): Am I qualified for a full monthly pension` (YMD 1940 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 10 FALSE
-- 65, not eligible for a full pension, 30 years of residence (at least ten, under forty).
#ASSERT `s 3(2): Am I qualified for a partial monthly pension` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 30 TRUE
-- Eligible for a full pension, so s 3(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): Am I qualified for a partial monthly pension` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 45 TRUE)
-- 5 years is under the ten the Act requires.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): Am I qualified for a partial monthly pension` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 5 TRUE)
-- A citizen the day before approval.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Not a citizen but legally resident the day before approval.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Ceased to live in Canada, and was legally resident the day before.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- Paragraph (b) needs the person to have ceased to live in Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- A pensioner on July 1, 1977 is not held to the requirement.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): Do I meet the requirement of legal residence for the pension` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Presumed: the Minister intends to waive, the prescribed information is there, no contrary evidence.
#ASSERT `s 4.1(a): Is my residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Contrary evidence defeats the presumption.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1(a): Is my residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- No intention to waive: no presumption.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1(a): Is my residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Actually met, whatever the presumption.
#ASSERT `s 4.1(a): Is my residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Presumed.
#ASSERT `s 4.1(b): Is my legal-residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Without the prescribed information there is no presumption.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1(b): Is my legal-residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Actually met.
#ASSERT `s 4.1(b): Is my legal-residence requirement treated as met when the Minister intends to waive my application` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Qualified, applied, approved.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 45 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- No application.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 45 TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not approved.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 45 TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- Not qualified.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me` (YMD 1960 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The day of approval itself.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me for a particular day` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE
-- The day before approval, nothing else allowing it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me for a particular day` (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE)
-- The day before approval, but another provision allows it.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): May a pension be paid to me for a particular day` (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2): Am I treated as having applied when my allowance ends at 65` TRUE TRUE
-- The Act says the Minister "may" deem: the Minister decides.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(2): Am I treated as having applied when my allowance ends at 65` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(2): Am I treated as having applied when my allowance ends at 65` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 5(2): On what day did I reach 65` (YMD 1960 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 15)
-- A census taken more than thirty years before the request.
#ASSERT `s 6: May the Minister obtain my age from census returns` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
-- Exactly thirty years is not "more than thirty years".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: May the Minister obtain my age from census returns` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1996 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
-- Not from census returns.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: May the Minister obtain my age from census returns` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)

§§ `Being in prison`
-- A sentence to be served in a penitentiary: (a).
#ASSERT `s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE
-- Over 90 days in a prison, the province having an agreement: (b).
#ASSERT `s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` TRUE FALSE 91 TRUE TRUE
-- Exactly 90 days does not exceed 90 days.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` TRUE FALSE 90 TRUE TRUE)
-- No agreement with the province.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` TRUE FALSE 91 TRUE FALSE)
-- Not in prison now.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): Am I an incarcerated person for whom no pension may be paid` FALSE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE)
-- Imprisoned from March 10; April is after the first month, and before the month of release.
#ASSERT `s 5(3): Is no pension payable to me for a month because I am in prison` (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20)
-- March is the first month of the period, which is excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): Is no pension payable to me for a month because I am in prison` (YMD 2026 3 20) TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20))
-- June is the month of release: ss 8(2.1) and 9.2 pay it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): Is no pension payable to me for a month because I am in prison` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20))
-- Not released yet: every month after the first is barred.
#ASSERT `s 5(3): Is no pension payable to me for a month because I am in prison` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE TRUE 800 FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 6 20)
-- Released June 20, notified: payment starts in respect of June.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): In respect of which month does my pension start if I am approved while in prison` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- No notice, no payment yet.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): In respect of which month does my pension start if I am approved while in prison` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not yet released.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): In respect of which month does my pension start if I am approved while in prison` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 20) TRUE (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not in prison at approval: the ordinary month governs.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): In respect of which month does my pension start if I am approved while in prison` FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.2: In respect of which month does my suspended pension resume after prison` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)
-- No notice, no resumption.
#ASSERT `s 9.2: In respect of which month does my suspended pension resume after prison` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not suspended for imprisonment.
#ASSERT `s 9.2: In respect of which month does my suspended pension resume after prison` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Applying, having my application waived, and withdrawing`
-- On the 65th birthday, the Minister satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 5(4): May the Minister waive my need to apply` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
-- The day before.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): May the Minister waive my need to apply` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE)
-- Not satisfied.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): May the Minister waive my need to apply` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 5(5): Am I owed written notice of the Minister's intention to waive my application` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(5): Am I owed written notice of the Minister's intention to waive my application` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 5(6): By what day must I correct inaccuracies in the Minister's information` (YMD 1961 10 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 9 30)
-- Nothing to correct.
#ASSERT `s 5(6): Have I met my duty to correct inaccuracies` (YMD 1961 10 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)
-- Filed on the last day.
#ASSERT `s 5(6): Have I met my duty to correct inaccuracies` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30)
-- Filed on the 65th birthday: too late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(6): Have I met my duty to correct inaccuracies` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1))
-- Not filed.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(6): Have I met my duty to correct inaccuracies` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1))
#ASSERT `s 5(7): Have I declined the waiver in time` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30)
-- On the 65th birthday is not before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(7): Have I declined the waiver in time` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(7): Have I declined the waiver in time` (YMD 1961 10 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 30))
#ASSERT `s 5(8): Am I required to make an application despite the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE
-- On or after the 65th birthday the Minister can no longer require it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): Am I required to make an application despite the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
-- No written notice.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): Am I required to make an application despite the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 5(4): Is the requirement that I apply waived` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): Is the requirement that I apply waived` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): Is the requirement that I apply waived` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): Is the requirement that I apply waived` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The day before payment commences.
#ASSERT `s 5.1(1): May I withdraw my application` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 31) (YMD 2026 11 1)
-- Payment has commenced.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(1): May I withdraw my application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2026 11 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(1): May I withdraw my application` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 31) (YMD 2026 11 1))
-- Never withdrawn.
#ASSERT `s 5.1(2): May my withdrawn application still be used` (YMD 2026 12 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- Used until the withdrawal.
#ASSERT `s 5.1(2): May my withdrawn application still be used` (YMD 2026 10 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 10 31)
-- Not after it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(2): May my withdrawn application still be used` (YMD 2026 11 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 10 31))

§ `How much pension, and when it is paid`

§§ `How much pension?`
-- 25 whole years of 40: 700 times 25/40.
#ASSERT `s 3(3): How much is my partial monthly pension` 700 25 EQUALS 437.5
-- 24.9 years is rounded to the lower multiple of a year (24): 700 times 24/40.
#ASSERT `s 3(3): How much is my partial monthly pension` 700 24.9 EQUALS 420
#ASSERT `s 3(4): How many whole years of residence count` 24.9 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `s 3(4): How many whole years of residence count` 25 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `s 3(4): How many whole years of residence count` 39.99 EQUALS 39
-- A period beginning after approval cannot raise the amount.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(5): May later residence increase my partial pension` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 1))
-- A period that began before approval is not barred.
#ASSERT `s 3(5): May later residence increase my partial pension` TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 10 1)
-- Not yet approved.
#ASSERT `s 3(5): May later residence increase my partial pension` FALSE (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 10 1)
-- The Act states one figure: January to March 1985.
#ASSERT `s 7(1): What does the Act itself say the full pension is for a month` (YMD 1985 2 14) EQUALS JUST 273.80
-- No other month: the later figures come from the quarterly adjustment (s 7(2)).
#ASSERT `s 7(1): What does the Act itself say the full pension is for a month` (YMD 1985 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1): What does the Act itself say the full pension is for a month` (YMD 2026 10 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No hold: 273.80 times 101/100.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): What is the full monthly pension after the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 4 1) 273.80 101 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 276.538
-- The index fell (99 against 100): no adjustment.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): What is the full monthly pension after the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 7 1) 273.80 99 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 273.80
-- A hold in force, the first index (102) above the carried 100: 273.80 times 102/100.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): What is the full monthly pension after the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1986 1 1) 273.80 102 95 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 279.276
-- A quarter must commence after March 31, 1985.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) to (4): What is the full monthly pension after the quarterly adjustment` (YMD 1985 3 31) 273.80 101 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The fall: the second index (100) is carried forward.
#ASSERT `s 7(4)(b): Which index figure is carried forward after a fall` (YMD 1985 7 1) 273.80 99 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 100
-- No fall, nothing carried.
#ASSERT `s 7(4)(b): Which index figure is carried forward after a fall` (YMD 1985 4 1) 273.80 101 100 FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Still not above 100: the base stays.
#ASSERT `s 7(4)(b): Which index figure is carried forward after a fall` (YMD 1985 10 1) 273.80 99.5 99 TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 100
-- 75 on May 15, 2021; the increase runs from July 2022.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): What is my pension after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2022 7 1) (YMD 1946 5 15) 700 EQUALS 770
-- Before the payment quarter commencing July 1, 2022.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): What is my pension after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2022 6 15) (YMD 1946 5 15) 700 EQUALS 700
-- The month of the 75th birthday is not increased.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): What is my pension after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2025 3 31) (YMD 1950 3 10) 700 EQUALS 700
-- The month after is.
#ASSERT `s 7(5): What is my pension after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 700 EQUALS 770
-- April 2020 to March 2021.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): For how many months is my pension increased for putting off my application` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 1955 3 15) 0 EQUALS 12
-- Two months excluded under (c).
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): For how many months is my pension increased for putting off my application` (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 10) (YMD 1955 3 15) 2 EQUALS 10
-- No month before July 2013: July 2013 to June 2014.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): For how many months is my pension increased for putting off my application` (YMD 2013 3 1) (YMD 2014 6 10) (YMD 1948 3 1) 0 EQUALS 12
-- No month after the month of the 70th birthday: April 2015 to March 2020.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(4): For how many months is my pension increased for putting off my application` (YMD 2015 3 10) (YMD 2021 1 5) (YMD 1950 3 10) 0 EQUALS 60
-- 0.6% of 700 is 4.20 a month; 12 months: 700 times 1.072.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): What is my full pension after the increase for putting off my application` 700 12 EQUALS 750.4
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): What is my full pension after the increase for putting off my application` 700 60 EQUALS 952
#ASSERT `s 7.1(1): What is my full pension after the increase for putting off my application` 700 0 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `s 7.1(2): What is my partial pension after the increase for putting off my application` 437.5 12 EQUALS 469
-- 750.40 times 1.10.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(5): What is my full pension, increased for putting off, after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 750.4 EQUALS 825.44
-- The month of the 75th birthday is not increased.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(5): What is my full pension, increased for putting off, after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 750.4 EQUALS 750.4
#ASSERT `s 7.1(6): What is my partial pension, increased for putting off, after the 10% increase at 75` (YMD 2025 4 1) (YMD 1950 3 10) 469 EQUALS 515.9
-- Qualified for a full pension only.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` TRUE 750.4 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST 750.4
-- The partial pension as increased is the greater of the two partial amounts.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` FALSE 0 TRUE 469 437.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 469
-- The greatest of the three.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` TRUE 500 TRUE 469 437.5 FALSE EQUALS JUST 500
-- The person decides otherwise: the Act does not say what they receive.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` TRUE 500 TRUE 469 437.5 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Qualified for no pension.
#ASSERT `s 7.1(3): What monthly pension am I to receive` FALSE 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `When is my pension paid, suspended, stopped or cancelled?`
-- No earlier day: the day of approval.
#ASSERT `s 8: As of which day is my approval effective` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 8 1)
-- 65 long before; a year before the day received is June 15, 2025: allowed (s 8(2)).
#ASSERT `s 8: As of which day is my approval effective` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 6 15)
-- A day before the later of (a) and (b): not allowed.
#ASSERT `s 8: As of which day is my approval effective` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 14) EQUALS (YMD 2026 8 1)
-- Under 65 when received: s 8(1) allows a day not before the day received.
#ASSERT `s 8: As of which day is my approval effective` (YMD 1962 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 6 20) EQUALS (YMD 2026 6 20)
-- Approved August 1: payment starts the first month after.
#ASSERT `s 8(1): In which month does my pension start` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 9 1)
-- Effective June 15, 2025: payment from the first month after, July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 8(1): In which month does my pension start` (YMD 1950 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 15) (YMD 2026 8 1) TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 7 1)
-- The pension ceases with the payment for the month of death.
#ASSERT `s 8(3): Is my pension still paid for a month` (YMD 2026 3 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(3): Is my pension still paid for a month` (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 20))
-- Lifetime.
#ASSERT `s 8(3): Is my pension still paid for a month` (YMD 2030 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 3 20)
-- Left March: April to September are the six months.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1) and (2): Is my pension suspended because I am outside Canada` (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 3 12) (YMD 2025 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 1) FALSE)
-- October is the first suspended month.
#ASSERT `s 9(1) and (2): Is my pension suspended because I am outside Canada` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 3 12) (YMD 2025 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 1) FALSE
-- Twenty years of residence: no suspension (s 9(2)).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1) and (2): Is my pension suspended because I am outside Canada` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 3 12) (YMD 2025 1 15) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 1) TRUE)
-- Payment may resume with the month of return.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1) and (2): Is my pension suspended because I am outside Canada` (YMD 2026 12 1) (YMD 2026 3 12) (YMD 2025 1 15) TRUE (YMD 2026 12 20) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3) and (4): Is my pension suspended because I ceased to live in Canada` (YMD 2026 9 30) (YMD 2026 3 12) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 5) FALSE)
-- Suspended six months after the end of March.
#ASSERT `s 9(3) and (4): Is my pension suspended because I ceased to live in Canada` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 3 12) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 5) FALSE
-- Twenty years: no suspension (s 9(4)).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3) and (4): Is my pension suspended because I ceased to live in Canada` (YMD 2026 10 1) (YMD 2026 3 12) FALSE (YMD 2026 12 5) TRUE)
-- Resumed in December: payment resumes with that month.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3) and (4): Is my pension suspended because I ceased to live in Canada` (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 3 12) TRUE (YMD 2026 12 5) FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 9(5): May my pension be suspended because I did not comply` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Resumed when complied.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(5): May my pension be suspended because I did not comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- The Act says "may": the Minister decides.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(5): May my pension be suspended because I did not comply` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- It ceases on the last day of the month of approval.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): On what day does my pension cease after I ask it to` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 12) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 31)
-- Not approved yet.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): On what day does my pension cease after I ask it to` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 3 12) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No request.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): On what day does my pension cease after I ask it to` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 3 12) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9.1(3): May I have my pension reinstated` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1(3): May I have my pension reinstated` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1(3): May I have my pension reinstated` TRUE FALSE)
-- The month following the month of the request.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): In which month does my reinstated pension start` (YMD 2026 4 10) FALSE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- The later of the following month and the month chosen.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): In which month does my reinstated pension start` (YMD 2026 4 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 7 15) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): In which month does my reinstated pension start` (YMD 2026 4 10) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` (YMD 2026 3 20) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` (YMD 2026 4 20) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT `s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` (YMD 2026 5 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 31) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT `s 9.1: Is my pension payable for a month after I asked to stop it` (YMD 2030 1 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 3 31) FALSE (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- Six months after July 1, 2026 is January 1, 2027.
#ASSERT `s 9.3(1): May I ask to cancel my pension` TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2027 1 1) 6
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): May I ask to cancel my pension` TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2027 1 2) 6)
-- Before payment commenced.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): May I ask to cancel my pension` TRUE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): May I ask to cancel my pension` FALSE (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 8 1) 6)
-- Repaid on the last day.
#ASSERT `s 9.3(2): Is my application treated as never made after I cancel` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2027 7 10) 6
-- A day late.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): Is my application treated as never made after I cancel` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2027 7 11) 6)
-- Not repaid.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): Is my application treated as never made after I cancel` TRUE (YMD 2027 1 10) FALSE (YMD 2027 7 10) 6)
-- Not granted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): Is my application treated as never made after I cancel` FALSE (YMD 2027 1 10) TRUE (YMD 2027 7 10) 6)

§ `Old Age Security Act, Part IV -- the questions about applying, appealing, being paid too much, and what the Minister may do`

§§ `Waiver, incapacity, death and error`
#ASSERT `s 26.1: On what day is my application deemed made once the requirement is waived` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 10 15)
#ASSERT `s 26.1: On what day is my application deemed made once the requirement is waived` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- November 2025 is 11 months before October 2026: not barred by this limit.
#ASSERT `s 26.1: May I be paid for a month before the waiver` (YMD 2025 11 1) (YMD 2026 10 15)
-- October 2025 is 12 months before: barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26.1: May I be paid for a month before the waiver` (YMD 2025 10 31) (YMD 2026 10 15))
#ASSERT `s 26.2: May the Minister collect and use my information to invite people to apply` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26.2: May the Minister collect and use my information to invite people to apply` FALSE)
-- The month before April 2026 is later than November 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): In which month may my application made for me be deemed made` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- The month incapacity commenced is the later.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): In which month may my application made for me be deemed made` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2026 4 2) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 1)
-- Not made on your behalf.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(1): In which month may my application made for me be deemed made` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Applied within the 20 days after recovering.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): In which month may my late application be deemed made after my incapacity` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 29) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- Too late: more than a month after the month in which you recovered, and more than the 20 days.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): In which month may my late application be deemed made after my incapacity` TRUE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 3 5) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 28.1(2): In which month may my late application be deemed made after my incapacity` FALSE (YMD 2026 1 10) 20 (YMD 2026 1 29) (YMD 2026 4 17) (YMD 2025 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
